  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MOROCCO Institutionalizing a Reform Process for the Business Environment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;This activity is the third phase of a three-phase comprehensive assistance program requested by the Moroccan authorities to improve Morocco&apos;s business environment through setting up an efficient reform process involving all public and private stakeholders. This framework has recently been established under phases 1 and 2 of the assistance program. It comprises: (i) a high level Public-Private Committee for the Business Environment chaired  by the Prime Minister, supported by working groups in charge of reform projects; (ii) a program management unit (PMU) in the MAEG ; (iii) a 2010 Reform Action Plan with 12 cross-cutting reform initiatives and performance indicators; and (iv) common &quot;&quot;reform guidelines&quot;&quot; for all involved stakeholders, detailing the different phases of the project cycle and supported by an IT tool easily accessible by stakeholders.  Under this third phase, the WB team will assist the Deputy Prime Minister Office for Economic and General Affairs (MAEG) in implementing and monitoring the reform program by: (a) Supporting the central &quot;&quot;Reform Management Unit (RMU)&quot;&quot; so that it is established as a credible facilitator of the reform process, and is able to monitor and follow up the reform progress; (b) Mobilizing technical expertise for preparing projects in various fields, i.e. legal, institutional, economic and financial ;(c) Setting up a Public-Private Dialogue (PPD) mechanism to build on the momentum for reform by launching a series of public-private consultations; (d) Evaluating results: The reform process needs to be periodically evaluated to be improved and adapted if necessary.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
